Article 10
(1) The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility in providing Protection to Women and Children Victims of Violence.
(2) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
a. implementing protection policies for women and children victims of violence established by the government;
b. establishing policies, programs, and activities for protection of women and children victims of violence;
c. collecting data and information about women and children victims of violence;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;
e. establishing PPT;
-10-
f. allocating budget in the implementation of Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence; and
g. fostering, supervising and evaluating the implementation of Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence.

